        ":question/problem": "The equation of the normal line to the curve $y = 2x^{2}$ at the point $(2, 8)$ is given by $x + py = q$ where $p$ and $q$ are constants. Find the value of $p + q$.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=2 x^{2}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(2 x^{2}\\right)=4 x\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(2,8):$\n\n$$\nm=f'(2)=8\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line is\n\n$$\nm'=-\\frac{1}{m}=- \\frac{1}{8}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(8)&=- \\frac{1}{8}(x-(2)) \\\\ x + 8 y&=66.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p+q=74.$",
